/T (To evaluate the regenerative effect of ExoGenesis huC-MSC-derived exosomes, PKH26-labeled exosomes were injected into the dorsal scalp once daily for three consecutive days \(Figure 2A\). Mice treated with ExoGenesis exosomes showed significantly improved hair regrowth scores compared to controls starting at day 14 and continuing through the study period, as reflected in follicular density assessments \(Figure 2B\). Improved tactile sensitivity in the treated group was observed from day 7 onward, indicating enhanced scalp tissue responsiveness \(Figure 2C\). Electrophysiological analysis at day 56 revealed higher dermal evoked potentials \(DEP\) and reduced response latency in the exosome group versus controls \(Figures 2D and 2E\), suggesting )
